# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## [2.0.12] – 2026-11-04
- RCO-2025 Vector Hub jobs (install and uninstall, service restart, certificate re-sync, live-channel poke) now run on the `HighPriorityQueue` instead of Laravel's default queue. No rConfig Horizon supervisor reads the `default` queue, so these jobs previously sat at "Queued" and never ran on servers without `REDIS_QUEUE` set, which blocked installing, restarting and re-syncing Vector Hub from the UI.

## [2.0.11] – 2026-11-03
- RCO-2020 The installer now pins the published Vector agent 2.0.1 release binary (SHA256 `1e28a22df13cfc6029992c51d1063dbbc700d75a03dbd9f460259fd39b88cb61`). The 2.0.10 installer pinned a pre-release build and refuses the published 2.0.1 binary with "not a known rConfig Vector agent release", so skip 2.0.10.
- Installer SHA256 for this release: `9a5de109f6761358ff7d11a3a6b34e5f4246f204d8bf2ad93a3580b4674df088`.

## [2.0.10] – 2026-11-03
- RCO-2020 Outbound source address: new nullable `agents.device_source_address` (IPv4 or IPv6), validated on agent create and update and sent to the agent in the sync response. An update that does not send the field leaves it unchanged. Loopback, link-local, unspecified, multicast and IPv4-mapped addresses are rejected, and the built-in agent (ID 1) cannot have one.
- RCO-2020 Agents report `source_address_status` at check-in (`ok`, `missing`, `invalid`, `unset`), stored as `agents.reported_source_address_status`. Agents before 2.0.1 leave it null.
- RCO-2020 `POST /api/v2/agents/provision` accepts `device_source_address` on create and returns `device_source_address` and `device_source_address_mismatch`. An existing agent's address is never changed.
- RCO-2020 Installer: `--instance <name>` installs one of several agents on a host (`/usr/local/bin/rconfig/agents/<name>`, templated `vectoragent@.service`, per-instance `VECTOR_AGENT_ROOT`), `--no-proxy` ignores host proxy variables, `--token-file` reads the bootstrap token from a file, and an installed agent can be updated without `--agent-id` or a token. Pins agent 2.0.1.
- Run the migration after upgrading. Agent create, update, sync and provision keep working before it has run.

## [2.0.9] – 2026-11-02
- RCO-1605 Vector Hub live-channel status is now refreshed from the hub when it is used, instead of relying only on the per-minute `vector:hub-sync-status` sync. A newly connected agent shows up within seconds.
- New `LiveChannelStatusService` holds the shared refresh logic, with a 10 second cache. `vector:hub-sync-status` now uses it and always polls the hub.
- New `GET vector-hub/agents/live-status` endpoint (`agent.view`) for polling. It returns `hub_reachable`, `checked_at` and each connected agent's `connected`, `rtt_ms` and `last_seen`, so the UI can show "unknown" rather than "disconnected" when the hub cannot be reached.
- `vector:access` checks the hub before listing agents and explains why none are selectable: hub unreachable, no agents connected, or connected agents not admin-enabled.

## [2.0.8] – 2026-10-27
- RCO-1848 Supports spatie/laravel-query-builder 7. The agent, agent log and agent queue lists no longer return a 500 on rConfig 8.4.1, which ships query-builder 7. Still works with query-builder 6.

## [2.0.7] – 2026-10-26
- The message printed by the retired `install.sh?bootstrap_token=` URL now points to the Vector Agents page in rConfig, instead of Settings > Agents, to find the new install command.

## [2.0.6] – 2026-10-26
- RCO-1830 Removed three agent routes that pointed at controller methods that never existed and returned a 500 when called: `POST api/agents/{id}/add-to-user`, `GET api/agents/active` and `GET api/agents/latest`. Nothing in rConfig called them.

## [2.0.5] – 2026-10-25
- RCO-1595 rConfig now sends a notification when a Vector agent goes down and again when it recovers. Requires rConfig 8.4.1 or later.

## [2.0.4] – 2026-10-25
- RCO-1817 **Breaking:** the Vector agent installer is now a static, verified script served from `GET /vector/agent-install.sh`, replacing the editable Blade template. Regenerate any saved or scripted install commands.
- The old `install.sh?bootstrap_token=` URL now prints where to find the new command and exits.
- Agent provisioning (UI and API v2) returns the new install command plus `installer_sha256` and `installer_docs_url`.
- RCO-1818 `vector:agent:download-binary` creates its folder as `0750`.

## [2.0.3] – 2026-10-25
- RCO-1794 New `VectorHubHelperCheck` service reports whether the root-owned Vector Hub helper is ready: the wrapper and its install script exist, are owned by root and writable by root only, and sudo lets the web user run the wrapper without a password (`sudo -n -l`).
- New config `vector-server.hub.install_script_path` (default `/usr/local/libexec/rconfig/rconfig-vector-hub-install.sh`).
- Vector Hub status API now returns `helper_installed`, `helper_problems` and `helper_fix`.
- Vector Hub install, uninstall, service restart and cert re-sync return a 422 naming the problem and the fix (`sudo php artisan rconfig:vector-hub-install-helper`) when the helper is not ready, instead of queuing a job that fails in Horizon.

## [2.0.2] – 2026-10-25
- RCO-1794 Vector Hub privileged actions (install, uninstall, service control) now run through a root-owned wrapper via `sudo -n` (new `VectorHubCtl` service, `vector-server.hub.ctl_path`) instead of `bash` or `systemctl` directly. Requires running rConfig's `rconfig:vector-hub-install-helper` as root after upgrading.
- `InstallVectorHubJob` takes an explicit `install` or `uninstall` action as its third argument.
- `SyncHubCertsJob` runs as the web user and reads hub certs through the `vector-hub` group.
- Install API: `insecure_download` is rejected and `rconfig_url`, `tunnel_host` and file paths are validated more strictly.
- Jobs use the `Process` facade.

## [2.0.1] – 2026-10-09
- Vector Access: the interactive device-access command is now `vector:access` (renamed from `vector:ssh`). This is a hard switch with no alias, so update any scripts or runbooks that call the old name. User-facing copy, the session transcript header, and the audit message are rebranded to "Vector Access"; internal identifiers (the `storage/logs/vector-ssh` path, the `vector_ssh_idle_timeout` setting, and the `live_ssh_session_logged` audit key) are unchanged.

## [2.0.0] – 2026-10-09
- RCO-744/RCO-1155 Vector Hub: bi-directional agent connectivity via a live channel. Hub API (IP + token auth, status/validation endpoints), `VectorHubClient`, and `vector:hub-sync-status` command.
- Vector Hub install and management from the UI (`InstallVectorHubJob`, `HubServiceActionJob`, hub routes), with self-healing hub client certificates (`SyncHubCertsJob`).
- Vector Access (`vector:access`): interactive terminal access to agent-connected devices through the hub, with session logging and a configurable idle timeout.
- Live job polling: new agent queue items poke the agent's live channel (`AgentQueueObserver`, `PokeAgentLiveChannelJob`) instead of waiting for the next poll.
- RCO-1250 Agent unit timeout clock now starts when the agent claims the unit (`claimed_at` column), not when it is queued.
- RCO-1253 Agent queue/notification hygiene fixes in `AgentQueueController`.
- RCO-1254 Vector dispatch observability: dispatch failures are now logged and reported instead of silently succeeding.
- New migrations: agents live channel, hub installs, SSH idle timeout setting, task run unit `claimed_at`. Run `php artisan migrate`.

## [1.3.2] – 2026-08-20
- closes RCO-1310 Device backup timeouts fired early on agent connected devices. The Device Connection Failure notification is now event driven, raised at the authoritative agent failure once retries are exhausted, instead of by the server side timeout watchdog which false positived on large agent fleets.
- An authoritative agent result now supersedes a unit previously marked with the speculative `TIMEOUT` status, and the run tracker counters are corrected when it does. `SUCCESS` and `FAILED` remain terminal, and `markUnitFailedByUlid` / `markUnitSuccessByUlid` now return whether they performed the transition so a notification fires exactly once per device.
- Failure notifications are dispatched outside the database transaction so mail dispatch no longer holds the queue row lock.
- Added `task_unit_timeout_seconds` (default 300) and `task_run_wait_timeout_seconds` (default 900) to `config/vector-server.php`, overridable with `VECTOR_TASK_UNIT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` and `VECTOR_TASK_RUN_WAIT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`.

